To apply the consumers.py fix and restart everything (redis + both celery workers + beat):
cd backend
.\start-docker.ps1
This runs docker compose up -d --build, which rebuilds any service whose image is stale and restarts it — Redis is unaffected since its image doesn't change.


If you just want to force-restart only the Celery workers (rebuild + recreate, skip touching Redis/Chroma):
cd backend
docker compose up -d --build celery-worker agent-worker celery-beat


Plain restart with no rebuild (only useful if you haven't changed backend code, e.g. just want a clean process):
docker compose restart celery-worker agent-worker celery-beat redis


Full stop/start cycle:
cd backend
.\start-docker.ps1 -Down
.\start-docker.ps1
